Architecture plan for Issue #128: Fix stale "25 MB" copy in the admin error boundary

Project shape:
- Next.js App Router application with TypeScript, React, Tailwind CSS, Prisma/PostgreSQL, and S3-compatible object storage.
- Public app routes live under app/(public); admin routes and admin server actions live under app/admin.
- Shared domain helpers live under lib/, reusable UI components under components/, and database schema/migrations under prisma/.

Relevant module/file organization:
- app/admin/error.tsx owns the admin error boundary UI and retry messaging.
- next.config.ts configures the server action/body size limit at 50mb.
- app/admin/posts/_components/post-upload-size-warning.tsx already communicates the 50 MB upload limit in the admin editor.

Issue dependency analysis:
- There is only one issue in this batch.
- It is an isolated copy-only fix with no schema, API, auth, storage, or routing dependencies.
- No shared types or new dependencies are needed.

Key design decisions:
- Update only the stale user-facing text in app/admin/error.tsx from 25 MB to 50 MB.
- Preserve the existing admin error boundary structure, styling, retry behavior, and logging behavior.
- Validate with a lightweight grep/test or lint if needed; full deployment should not require database or storage changes.
